### Test file for POService (run with cds watch running on port 4004)

### 1. All purchase orders
GET http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/po/PurchaseOrders

### 2. Late POs (due date in the past and not fully delivered)
GET http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/po/PurchaseOrders?$filter=dueDate%20lt%202026-11-03%20and%20deliveredQty%20lt%20orderedQty&$expand=vendor

### 3. Sorted by due date
GET http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/po/PurchaseOrders?$orderby=dueDate

### 4. With vendor details
GET http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/po/PurchaseOrders?$expand=vendor

### 5. Create with amount 0 (expect 400)
POST http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/po/PurchaseOrders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "poNumber": "4500098",
  "vendor_ID": "V001",
  "dueDate": "2026-12-15",
  "orderedQty": 10,
  "deliveredQty": 0,
  "amount": 0
}

### 6. Create a valid PO (expect 201)
POST http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/po/PurchaseOrders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "poNumber": "4500099",
  "vendor_ID": "V001",
  "dueDate": "2026-12-15",
  "orderedQty": 10,
  "deliveredQty": 0,
  "amount": 5000.00
}
